  "articleBody": "Picking out new flooring for your kitchen can feel like a big decision, and it totally is! You want something that looks great but also stands up to daily life in a busy kitchen. One of the biggest things to think about is moisture. Is the flooring truly waterproof or just water-resistant? That's a huge difference when you're dealing with spills and potential leaks. You'll also want to know exactly what's included in any quote you get — things like subfloor prep, appliance removal, and debris haul-away can add up if they're not explicitly stated. And don't forget about durability and how easy it is to clean. Kitchens see a lot of foot traffic and spills, so a low-maintenance, tough material is usually a winner. Finally, think about the existing subfloor; some materials work better with certain subfloors than others. If you're unsure about any of these points, it's always smart to chat with a professional who can help you weigh your options and make the best choice for your home. We're always here to help guide you through the process.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}